# Kraken API credentials -- used by kraken/client.py for authenticated
# (private) endpoints: checking your USD/asset balances and placing orders
# via kraken/propose_order.py --execute. Public data (AssetPairs, Ticker,
# OHLC -- everything discovery, backtesting, and paper trading use) needs no
# key at all, so backtest/backtest_all.py and paper_trading/run_paper_cycle.py
# both run fine with this file left blank.
#
# Copy this file to .env (already gitignored -- never commit the real one)
# and fill in both values yourself in a local text editor. See
# docs/KRAKEN_SETUP.md for how to create a key with the right permissions.
#
# Same philosophy as the rest of this project (see CLAUDE.md): fund the
# Kraken account with only money you're willing to lose, and scope the key's
# permissions as narrowly as Kraken allows (Query Funds + Create/Modify
# Orders -- NEVER enable Withdraw Funds on this key).

# From Kraken's Settings -> API page. KRAKEN_API_SECRET is the base64-encoded
# "Private Key" Kraken shows you once at creation time -- copy it immediately,
# Kraken will not show it again.
KRAKEN_API_KEY=
KRAKEN_API_SECRET=
